can take a varied number of arguments and return a varied number of results. Only }{\b IOCTL_ACPI_EVAL_METHOD }{is documented here because of the similarity of the two IOCTLs.
\par When }{\b IOCTL_ACPI_EVAL_METHOD}{ is sent to the ACPI device object through a call to }{\b IoCallDriver}{
, a pointer to IO_STACK_LOCATION is obtained and then a method is called to handle the IOCTL synchronously. The argument list is parsed and the request in an IRP is converted into the structures required by the AML Interpreter.
